    "An attacker may be able to manipulate parameters to exploit vulnerabilities in the server's processing of other structured data formats, such as a JSON or XML. To test for this, inject unexpected structured data into user inputs and see how the server responds." => 'Masukan pengguna yang disisipkan langsung ke struktur JSON atau XML menuju API internal juga berisiko menyuntikkan properti tambahan.',
    'Consider an application that enables users to edit their profile, then applies their changes with a request to a server-side API. When you edit your name, your browser makes the following request:' => 'Misalnya pembaruan profil mengirim nilai formulir biasa dari klien:',
    'You can attempt to add the [[C0]] parameter to the request as follows:' => 'Penyerang dapat menyisipkan tanda kutip penutup untuk menambah properti [[C0]]:',
    'If the user input is added to the server-side JSON data without adequate validation or sanitization, this results in the following server-side request:' => 'Tanpa encoding JSON yang benar, payload JSON internal di backend berubah menjadi:',
    'This may result in the user [[C0]] being given administrator access.' => 'Akibatnya, akun [[C0]] memperoleh peran administrator.',
    'Consider a similar example, but where the client-side user input is in JSON data. When you edit your name, your browser makes the following request:' => 'Hal serupa terjadi ketika masukan klien sudah berbentuk JSON lalu di-decode terlebih dahulu sebelum digabungkan ke string JSON internal:',
    'If the user input is decoded, then added to the server-side JSON data without adequate encoding, this results in the following server-side request:' => 'Setelah string JSON di-decode di frontend lalu ditempel langsung ke badan permintaan backend, properti tambahan tetap ikut tereksekusi:',
    'Again, this may result in the user [[C0]] being given administrator access.' => 'Dengan begitu, akun [[C0]] kembali berpeluang memperoleh hak akses administrator.',
    'Structured format injection can also occur in responses. For example, this can occur if user input is stored securely in a database, then embedded into a JSON response from a back-end API without adequate encoding. You can usually detect and exploit structured format injection in responses in the same way you can in requests.' => 'Injeksi format terstruktur juga dapat terjadi saat data tersimpan ditempel ke respons JSON tanpa escaping memadai.',
    'This example below is in JSON, but server-side parameter pollution can occur in any structured data format. For an example in XML, see the [[A0]]XInclude attacks[[/A0]] section in the XML external entity (XXE) injection topic.' => 'Selain JSON, injeksi pada XML dibahas melalui teknik [[A0]]serangan XInclude[[/A0]] di topik XXE.',
    'Testing with automated tools' => 'Pengujian dengan alat otomatis',
    'Burp includes automated tools that can help you detect server-side parameter pollution vulnerabilities.' => 'Beberapa fitur otomatis dapat membantu mendeteksi transformasi parameter mencurigakan selama audit.',
    "Burp Scanner automatically detects suspicious input transformations when performing an audit. These occur when an application receives user input, transforms it in some way, then performs further processing on the result. This behavior doesn't necessarily constitute a vulnerability, so you'll need to do further testing using the manual techniques outlined above. For more information, see the [[A0]]Suspicious input transformation[[/A0]] issue definition." => 'Burp Scanner menandai temuan [[A0]]Suspicious input transformation[[/A0]] yang perlu diverifikasi ulang dengan metode manual di atas.',
    "You can also use the Backslash Powered Scanner BApp to identify server-side injection vulnerabilities. The scanner classifies inputs as boring, interesting, or vulnerable. You'll need to investigate interesting inputs using the manual techniques outlined above. For more information, see the [[A0]]Backslash Powered Scanning: hunting unknown vulnerability classes[[/A0]] whitepaper." => 'Ekstensi Backslash Powered Scanner (lihat riset [[A0]]Backslash Powered Scanning[[/A0]]) juga memetakan masukan menarik yang berpotensi disuntikkan ke backend.',
    'Preventing server-side parameter pollution' => 'Mencegah server-side parameter pollution',
    "To prevent server-side parameter pollution, use an allowlist to define characters that don't need encoding, and make sure all other user input is encoded before it's included in a server-side request. You should also make sure that all input adheres to the expected format and structure." => 'Selalu enkode masukan pengguna sesuai konteks (URL, JSON, atau XML) memakai pembangun struktur data standar serta validasikan terhadap format yang diharapkan sebelum dikirim ke API internal.',

